WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.720
Look, Ren. Those are real raccoon dogs.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.850
Apparently raccoon dogs 
are canines, just like dogs.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.780
Raccoon dogs live very close to us

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.470
Anyway, I had no idea there was a zoo nearby.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:17.740
Right?

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.450
I knew if we were going to live together, 
it'd have to be near here.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.960
Tokyo's too much of a big city 
for a kid who grew up in Canada.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.850
That's not true. I'll get used to it.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.620
I guess you're right.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.030
It's already been six months since 
you moved to Japan from Canada.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.730
Haru, you should go back once in a while.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.910
The dogs, and Rob and Fumie, miss you.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.240
What are you doing?

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.580
Your nails are getting long.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.860
I'll cut them for you when we get home.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.520
I can cut my nails myself!

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.160
But you always cut them too 
short when you do it yourself.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.650
I can cut them how I want!

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.330
<i>It's been a year since I started living with Haru.</i>

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:05.350
It looks painful. I don't like seeing it.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.050
<i>But...</i>

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:06.700
Okay?

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.550
<i>Just recently, I've realized 
that his shady smile</i>

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:14.060
<i>and overprotective habits are 
unbelievably true to who he actually is.</i>

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.180
Bro, where are you right now?

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.450
Where am I?

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.320
Some weird lady is at the house.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.730
She said to tell you "Kiyoka" 
and you'd figure it out.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.140
Oh, sorry!

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.110
Aki, I'll be right home.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.190
Let her in and serve her 
some tea or something.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:32.940
What?

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.120
Bro?

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.870
Damn! He hung up.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.440
Is she his girlfriend?

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.620
Is that the type he's into?

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:46.530
Well, he's always had poor taste in women...

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.730
You're not one to talk.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.760
You're late!

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:29.230
Kiyo! Sorry, I totally forgot you were coming.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:30.270
Wait, what?

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.080
Why are you outside?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.150
Beats me!

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.270
Your twin brothers apparently 
didn't want to let me inside!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:38.910
So you do know her?

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:43.690
I told you before that someone else 
would be running the bar at night.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.460
This is her. Takamori...

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.280
Kiyoka. Nice to meet you.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.970
Oh, these are my twin brothers...

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.170
I know.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.260
Your twin brothers, Aki and Shima, right?

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.170
Haru and I were classmates in high school.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.290
I've listened to Haru brag about 
his brothers more than enough.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.880
I can't help but remember.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.510
But he never told me anything

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:11.160
about his third brother.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.050
That's Ren, the youngest.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.660
Ren?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.420
I'm taking Tanuki for a walk.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.630
Don't go too far.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.570
Don't follow any strange people or dogs.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.250
Ugh, this guy hasn't changed at all...

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.100
<i>The youngest, huh?</i>

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.190
So Kiyoka-san, you've known 
our brother since high school?

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.130
Yeah.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.920
I was surprised when I ran into 
him in Kabukicho, though.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.960
He disappeared after he quit high school.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.520
He'd turn up every once in a while,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.280
but I thought he was out of his mind when he said

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.860
he wanted to open a café during the day.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.890
Listen, Kiyo...

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.980
Do you think you could stop 
insulting me in front of my brothers?

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.980
Those aren't insults!

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:05.990
Your stupid desire to close shop 
in time for dinner is the reason

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.670
I have to be your partner!

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:12.750
And then there's Iku. He's so 
devoted to you, he quit the club.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:14.860
"We're opening a café."

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.820
I wish she'd insulted him some more.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:18.250
"I hope we get lots of cute customers," he said.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:17.640
Yeah.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.740
You think the world's that easy, you upstarts?!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.090
I'm sorry...

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.460
You don't seem to be having much fun.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.130
Oh, my.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.460
What a timid dog.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.480
Is this his first walk?

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.580
It is for me, but I'm not sure about him.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.530
I'm just taking care of him for a friend.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.910
He'd started living under
the porch at some point.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:52.630
Oh, my.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:57.750
Cocoa, what's wrong with you?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:02.320
He's probably scared because 
I was raised alongside large dogs.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.190
Their smell may still be on me.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.130
Really?

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.830
Is he a Pomeranian?

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.310
I'm not sure.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:16.470
But if he was found under the porch, 
does that mean he was lost?

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.840
His real owners might be 
looking for him right now.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.780
<i>His real owners...</i>

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:27.440
I get the picture, more or less.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:30.660
But don't you think this estimate is too low?

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:34.040
Iku and I will help in whatever way we can.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.870
You're as shrewd as ever.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.540
What about a refrigerator and cookware?

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.910
My friend's closing his store, so he said 
we could take whatever we wanted.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:47.170
You're so lucky, I wish 
I could put a curse on you.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.620
Well, I'm leaving.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.660
I'll be stopping by again, 
so don't slack off.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.210
I'll do my best.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.010
Can I give you a ride?

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.520
No, thanks.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.120
So hungry...

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:03.270
So hungry...

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.270
I can't take a househusband away 
from his family before dinner.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:04.770
Sorry.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:07.400
Oh, right, Haru...

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.460
Do you remember her?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.990
Her?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.350
She comes to drink at my bar sometimes.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:18.240
But wasn't that six years ago?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.700
So I figured it'd be okay now, and told her—

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.540
Don't tell her anything else.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:27.350
I only told her I saw you around town.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.800
But she's really looking for you, so here. 
It's her contact information.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:36.230
Things are different now. 
Why don't you go see her?

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.610
She's an adult, and so are you.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.990
I think a kind, older woman would 
be a good match for you, though.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.580
What are you looking at? Cheeky brat.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:55.410
It's no wonder Haru can't be free.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:59.790
I can't believe he's looking after a child 
like you just because you're his brother.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:01.820
<i>She's right.</i>

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.120
<i>On top of that, I'm not his brother.</i>

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:09.410
<i>At least... I don't think...</i>

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.510
Haru?

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.540
Ah, you found me.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:19.030
Your homeroom teacher asked to see me.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:23.480
Seems he's worried about 
how naïve you are, too.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.190
Me? How am I naïve?

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:29.600
He was laughing because you haven't 
experienced karaoke or arcades yet.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.190
I'm partly responsible for that.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.750
Are those necessary?

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.080
Think of it as a rite of passage.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.940
If you want to be a normal 
high school student, at least.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.350
I am normal.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:42.200
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:46.730
Anyway, I heard you only take notes 
in your modern Japanese class?

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.670
Is that wrong?

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:51.480
I thought your classes might be too easy for you.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:55.220
Has Haruko-san been teaching you until now?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.220
Wasn't it the same for you?

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:02.950
Plus, Haruko's old friends would 
always give me lectures online.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.280
Old friends? You mean her CERN friends?

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.230
European Organization for Nuclear Research

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:06.140
Yeah.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:10.030
Isn't Haruko back at the research facility now?

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.950
<i>Wh-What am I supposed to do with him?</i>

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.220
Haruko said it'd be easier down the road

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:20.490
if I learned up to college-level 
physics and math early.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.840
<i>"College-level" means Harvard level 
to Haruko-san, doesn't it?</i>

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:28.010
<i>And eight thousand of the world's 
top physicists working at CERN</i>

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.480
<i>have been giving him private 
lessons since he was a kid?!</i>

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:32.460
Haru?

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.130
<i>What the hell was she thinking?</i>

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.310
Then the classes here must bore you, right?

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.630
I'm fine.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:49.020
And starting next month, they're putting 
together a special curriculum that involves

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.520
inviting college professors here 
for a few hours each week.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:55.780
Really? I'm glad Mikiko-san 
recommended I send you here.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:57.970
Haru...

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:58.990
What?

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.640
I think Tanuki might have real owners.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:07.090
Maybe, but you haven't found them yet, right?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.460
You're so cute, Ren!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.880
Is that why you've been so gloomy?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.160
You've been spending a lot 
of time with Tanuki lately!

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.370
Who's more important to you, me or him?

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:24.160
Shut up!

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.890
Come to think of it, I still haven't

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.030
gotten my goodbye kiss for this morning!

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:28.970
Move, pervert!

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.610
I'm not a pervert. I'm your brother!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.440
What the hell? Talk about 
an embarrassing couple...

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:31.390
Stop!

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:33.900
Come on, Ren! You can give me 
my morning kiss now!

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:36.910
Huh. Considering the rent...

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.580
It's pretty nice, right?

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.160
Are you okay with construction 
starting after Golden Week?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.820
Sure, but until it opens,

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:49.030
remember that you two are just deadbeats.

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:50.410
It's okay.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:53.390
If I run into money problems, 
I plan on joining their family.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:54.970
You have to work, Iku.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.950
Huh? Man, I'm hungry...

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.130
Me, too.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:02.000
You two are such babies.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.580
Haru, did you try calling her?

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.780
Why would I?

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.100
Because I know

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.060
what you were like then.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:18.030
She was the first girl you 
really loved, wasn't she?

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:21.000
She was older, but you couldn't leave her be.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.070
The only woman you were ever selfish with.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.700
But in the end, she wouldn't listen.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.580
You still can't forget her, can you?

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:33.400
That was six years ago.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.270
Yeah, but it's okay.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:40.450
You don't have the willpower to get over her.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:45.420
Ow!

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.080
Give me those. I'll do it.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:51.390
Haru?

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:53.940
Sorry I forgot about this.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.160
I can do it myself.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.360
You always cut them too short.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.980
Give me your right hand.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:03.110
You're too clumsy to do it.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.110
Shut up!

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:06.620
Your hands are so small.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.640
Iku!

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:18.740
Wh-Wh-What is it?!

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.130
What the hell is going on 
between those brothers?!

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.970
Huh? I guess it even shocked you—

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.970
I won't stand for that incestuous relationship!

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:30.220
But they're not related by blood!

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.390
Huh?

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:34.290
Really?

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:38.500
Then there's no reason Haru has 
to take care of him, is there?

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:42.200
His parents adopted him 
before they passed away.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.110
Haru-san won't let Ren Ren go.

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:46.500
Why not?

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:48.620
It's complicated.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:53.290
If Haru-san were to let Ren Ren go, 
he'd be sent to an orphanage.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:57.130
He doesn't want him to go 
through what he experienced!

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.880
Why are you crying?

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:05.210
Because you're talking about 
Ren Ren like he's a nuisance!

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.560
And anyone would cry if they got stepped on!

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:13.640
There's a bar counter I have my eye on.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:17.650
That's your choice, 
but I'm not paying anything for it.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:20.440
Cheapskate! You made tons of money as a host!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.900
Well, how many businesses 
have you opened at your age?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.280
Four!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:29.210
People keep asking me to 
help them open their stores!

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:30.530
Ren, sorry.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.040
I need to take some measurements at the café.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.100
Could you clean up for me?

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:36.690
Okay.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.840
Hey, do you like Haru?

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.250
Is that any of your business?

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:47.840
It is.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:52.440
I once confessed my feelings 
to Haru, and he rejected me.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:55.810
So what? It's still none of your business.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.540
Haru divides people into three categories.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:04.530
Family, brothers, and others. Pretty broad, right?

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.690
But there's someone who doesn't 
fit into any of those categories.

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:12.290
After meeting her, Haru changed a lot.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.030
How?

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.470
It's a secret. I'm not telling you.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:20.450
In any case, she really wants to see Haru now.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.800
Then Haru should see her, if he wants to.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.550
Are you sure you're okay with that?

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.960
He's a womanizer to the core.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:31.050
I know.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.770
No way! Do you actually like Haru?

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:35.110
Even though you're his brother?

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:36.430
I'm not his brother.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.220
Let me correct myself, then.

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:43.150
Even though you're a boy, 
a child, and his brother?

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:50.990
Kunisue Miki

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:50.990
Haru...

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.730
It's okay.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:56.250
It's good to have more family.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.250
Haru?

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.110
How long are you going to keep drinking?

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:04.000
Oh... Ren, sorry. What time is it?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.070
It's long past midnight.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:09.510
Really? Let's stay up all night together, then.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:11.010
Want to watch a movie?

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:14.280
You're always telling me to go to bed early.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.800
Staying up late with Ren...

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.060
You reek of booze!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:23.000
Hey, Shima recorded something.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.100
Is this okay?

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.520
Anything's fine.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:35.240
A pretty girl can get a teenage boy to do a lot of things.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:33.830
A pretty girl can get a teenage 
boy to do a lot of things.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.870
Are you like that, too, Haru?

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:47.130
Sweat       Sweat

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.770
Where did that come from?

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:45.370
Kiyoka said you're a womanizer to the core.

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.130
<i>I wish my dark past would disappear!</i>

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:51.270
She also said the woman who 
changed you wants to see you.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:52.510
Are you going to?

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:54.580
No.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:55.820
Why not?

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.680
I have you.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.180
I have nothing to do with it.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.270
But you do.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:04.610
Don't force the blame onto me!

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:05.270
Ren?

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:09.030
Do you work, live in a big house, make dinner,

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:12.070
and go to the zoo just for me?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.160
Because I'm here?

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.930
Of course! What's wrong with that?

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:18.790
You said you wanted to live with me, so I—

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:22.410
I don't want you to do anything 
you don't want to do!

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:25.090
What I want?

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:28.630
That's why you're an idiot.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:29.880
Hey, Ren!

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:33.060
I'm sleeping in my room tonight.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:40.800
<i>What's his deal?</i>

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.490
<i>He's been sleeping in my room until this morning</i>

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:45.600
<i>because he doesn't like sleeping alone.</i>

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.110
Tanuki?

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.990
Sorry, it's not Tanuki.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.120
You want me to do what I want?

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:05.520
Haru?

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.380
Haru!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.590
This is what you wanted.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:15.510
You said you only wanted me to do what I wanted.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:20.600
so I'm not letting your precious 
dog in this room anymore.

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:21.620
Move!

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:22.680
I won't listen.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.920
Don't touch me!

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:24.600
No.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.240
<i>I don't know this man.</i>

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.870
<i>Haru's not being his usual cheerful self.</i>

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:38.270
<i>I don't know this man who's ignoring what I say.</i>

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:40.830
<i>I don't know this scary man.</i>

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.170
Did you bite my tongue?!

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:50.060
Serves you right, you drunk.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:52.670
It's your fault for not being able 
to hold your liquor at your age.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:18:00.030
You're right. Sorry for getting 
drunk and acting like this.

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:03.750
Haru?

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.920
I was kidding.

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:13.220
As if I'd ever actually make a 
move on my little brother.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:18.530
<i>Shit.</i>

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.170
Really?

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:23.400
<i>No, not really! Tell him, quick!</i>

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.640
I'm sorry.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:28.540
<i>Why is Ren apologizing?</i>

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.250
Bro, are you hungover?

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.780
You and Ren were up late 
making a lot of noise.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:41.180
Did you have a fight?

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:44.170
Like I'd ever fight with Ren.

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:48.310
I guess... But Ren left early this morning.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.190
To go where?

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:52.760
Who knows? He took Tanuki with him, 
so he probably went for a walk.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:54.440
But it's already noon.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.560
He can handle himself. 
You do give him an allowance.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:00.840
Shima, call Ren's phone.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.710
Okay.

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:04.580
His phone's right here.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:23.930
He's not here...

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.930
I ended up circling the park three times.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.940
Where the hell is Ren?

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:36.070
Really? I'm sorry.

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:39.930
<i>I didn't mean to make him say that.</i>

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:41.070
Haru?

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:44.580
What's wrong? Why are you drenched in sweat?

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.600
<i>Why is he behaving normally?</i>

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:51.190
I just thought I'd go for a run.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:54.190
Anyway, where have you been all morning?

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:57.130
Looking for Tanuki's owners 
around the old man's house.

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:58.460
What?

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.130
Wouldn't you feel bad for his original owners, 
and Tanuki, if they were looking for him?

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:04.640
So did you find them?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:05.690
Sort of.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:06.740
Sort of?

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:11.140
His owner was a senior living alone 
who passed away last month.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:17.680
I think he started living at the old man's 
place because he resembled his owner.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:19.560
I see...

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:22.150
It's sad, but it can't be helped.

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.520
Anyway, Ren, you must be hungry.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:27.120
Let's get you home and—

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:30.710
Ren?

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:33.490
I'm not hungry.

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:34.540
I see.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:40.380
Hey, Ren. Why did you bother 
to look for Tanuki's owners?

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:43.090
I understand how it feels to not have a home.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:44.390
I'm just like him.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:47.890
If you have a home, wouldn't you 
be happier going back there?

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.830
To not have a home?

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:53.390
Ren, you dummy. You do have a home.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:56.270
<i>No. I made him say this.</i>

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:59.270
You're right. Thank you.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:04.320
There's a big cherry tree in front of your window,

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:05.470
so...

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:08.200
Yeah, it was beautiful.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.730
Even if I move out someday, 
I'll never forget it.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.040
Haru...

00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:14.050
What?

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:16.540
<i>Damn it! All of this is starting 
to make my head hurt.</i>

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:18.370
Sorry about yesterday.

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:20.300
Why are you apologizing first?

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:23.390
I shouldn't have said all those things.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.370
I don't know how to maintain an appropriate 
distance from you like Aki and Shima.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:30.940
I always get too close and end up hurting you.

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:32.070
But that's—

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:34.990
I know. Because I'm not your real brother.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:38.180
Ren, it's not like that.

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:40.940
If you want me to, I'll try harder.

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:45.450
If you want me to, I'll be just your brother.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:49.950
So you don't have to worry about me 
more than necessary anymore.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:58.720
<i>I made him say this, too.</i>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Next Time
